{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1402587-dark-tides-rising","id":1402587,"title":"Dark Tides Rising","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-13T06:28:53-07:00","id":1402587,"title":"Dark Tides Rising","content":"I really liked this book. I\u2019m looking forward to reading (and maybe eventually playing) Son of the Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T08:05:37-07:00","id":1402602,"title":"","content":"I recently started running a Transylvania Chronicles game using DAV20 rules. It's pretty slow-going at this point; I'm the only one really familiar with the game, and even I have zero play experience. But so far we seem to be having fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I can't remember the precise name, but there's a blog where someone reviews all 12 Acts, plus TbN for background. I agree with a lot of the criticisms around excessive railroading at times and NPCs having a bad habit of outshining the cast, but it's an interesting myth arc that lets you be part of so much of VtM's history <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Worth some tinkering to get it running ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T12:44:18-07:00","id":1402659,"title":"","content":"Thank you \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-13T13:42:25-07:00","id":1402672,"title":"","content":"In fairness, if you have a story which allows the characters to be a part of some of the key events of Cainite / Kindred history, they will inevitably spend a lot of time surrounded by characters who outclass them in terms of raw power, or age. There's simply no way to avoid that. I've never got to play the Transylvania Chronicles but I love them for the deep delve into the heart of the lore. They're a different type of game from most with different goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}